<p>There I was, drafting an email reply in macOS 27.2.1, when I was greeted by this fresh hell:</p>
<figure><img height="1020" sizes="(max-width: 1010px) calc(100vw - 60px), 690px" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-ai-6c.png?ssl=1&amp;w=690&amp;quality=90 690w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-ai-6c.png?ssl=1&amp;w=1035&amp;quality=90 1035w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-ai-6c.png?ssl=1&amp;w=1380&amp;quality=90 1380w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-ai-6c.png?ssl=1&amp;w=2070&amp;quality=90 2070w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-ai-6c.png?ssl=1&amp;w=2760&amp;quality=90 2760w" width="1670" data-recalc-dims="1" decoding="async" src="https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-ai-6c.png?ssl=1&#038;w=1380&#038;quality=90" alt="An email draft with a message about using artificial intelligence to write a short sentence." /><figcaption></figcaption></figure>
<p>I&#8217;ve been <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/09/ios-27-review-little-things-mean-a-lot/">on record since the 27 releases</a> as saying that I find Siri&#8217;s writing tools across the platform updates to be unnecessarily aggressive, and they certainly haven&#8217;t gotten less so.</p>
<p>Look, I&#8217;m a professional writer. I do not need help writing a three-sentence email. If there are people who find these features useful, have at! But I would love the ability to dispatch them with extreme prejudice, and I can find no options anywhere in Mail to say &#8220;begone with you!&#8221;</p>
<p>But all hope is not lost. After complaining on Mastodon<sup id="fnref-42464-paternity"><a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/11/get-rid-of-siri-ais-aggressive-writing-controls-in-mail/#fn-42464-paternity" class="jetpack-footnote" title="Read footnote.">1</a></sup>, Andrew Kemp offered this suggestion:</p>
<blockquote class="mastodon-embed" data-embed-url="https://mastodon.social/@ajwk/117645583843489938/embed" style="background: #FCF8FF; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #C9C4DA; margin: 0; max-width: 540px; min-width: 270px; overflow: hidden; padding: 0;"></blockquote>
<p><script data-allowed-prefixes="https://mastodon.social/" async src="https://mastodon.social/embed.js"></script></p>
<p>Lo and behold, yes! If you open up System Settings and go to Screen Time > Content &amp; Privacy, then turn on the Content &amp; Privacy switch, you can <em>then</em> go into the Siri sub-menu and turn off Writing Assistance. (You can also disable other Siri options in here, such as Broad World Knowledge, Image Creation, and Realistic Images, all of which probably make more sense for the parental controls for which Screen Time is designed.)</p>
<p>I had to close and re-open my draft message, but when I did, it was back to just the formatting bar. Phew.</p>
<figure><img height="1020" sizes="(max-width: 1010px) calc(100vw - 60px), 690px" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-2026-6c.png?ssl=1&amp;w=690&amp;quality=90 690w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-2026-6c.png?ssl=1&amp;w=1035&amp;quality=90 1035w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-2026-6c.png?ssl=1&amp;w=1380&amp;quality=90 1380w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-2026-6c.png?ssl=1&amp;w=2070&amp;quality=90 2070w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-2026-6c.png?ssl=1&amp;w=2760&amp;quality=90 2760w" width="1670" data-recalc-dims="1" decoding="async" src="https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/email-draft-2026-6c.png?ssl=1&#038;w=1380&#038;quality=90" alt="An email draft with the subject 'To:'. The body contains a message about using artificial intelligence to draft short sentences because the writer is lazy." /><figcaption></figcaption></figure>
<p>I don&#8217;t love having to turn to Screen Time for this feature any more than I like the idea of using accessibility features for aesthetic alterations to the OS, but any port in a storm, I suppose.</p>
<p>I know we&#8217;re in the era of &#8220;shove AI into everything!&#8221; but I have generally appreciated Apple&#8217;s more conservative stance here. I just wish they would give us more granular options for turning off the parts of these features we don&#8217;t want that doesn&#8217;t require parenting ourselves.</p>
